Today I solved leetcode question 3550:Smallest Index with the digit sum equal to index.
Description: Problem states that we are given an array of integers.
              We must find the smallest index where digit sum of that number is equal to index of that number.
              If we don't find any of the number then the answer will be -1.
              eg- arr=[1,10,11]
                  So at index 0 digit sum of number is 1.
                  At index 1 digit sum of 10 is 1. So 1 will be our answer.
Solution: We start our loop from 0th index.
          Then we can make another variable named num with same value as the number at that index.
          And we will make another variable named sum with the value 0.
          Then we will start a while loop which will check if our num is greater than 0.
          And we will add digits to sum by taking modulo by 10 of num.
          And we will divide num by 10.
          And when while loop ends we will check if sum is equal to current index or not.
          And if yes then we will retuen that index.
          When we exit our main loop and till that time if we haven't found our answer then we can return -1.
